From 14e01be8494719a3337bfd2dbdc3a60f4883b025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:04:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): name the native wire EDM post without the machine
 brand

The wire post "Agie native wire EDM" is now "Native wire EDM job files",
one constant (posting::agie::POST). The old name stays a hidden alias
(posting::agie::LEGACY_POST): a saved project, an option key
builtin:<name>, a script, an MCP call or a machine file that uses it
selects the post, and the world and new files store the new name.

Refusals and UI texts say what is wrong with the job, not which machine
brand needs it. The 11 agie-native .refusal goldens change with the .cps
throw text. No posted program changes.

Fixes #3537

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
